    <channel>
        <title>DuoUpdater</title>
        <!--
          The Sparkle feed. `scripts/publish-release.sh` regenerates this file on
          every release and pushes it here. The app reads it through
          https://updates.duoupdater.app/appcast.xml (workers/appcast relays this
          file); builds before that read
          https://raw.githubusercontent.com/jizhi0v0/duo-updater/main/appcast.xml
          directly, so this path must keep working.

          Deliberately empty rather than absent: an appcast with no items means
          "nothing newer available", which Sparkle handles as up-to-date, whereas
          a missing file is a fetch error on every check. The first release fills
          it in.

          Release history starts here. Earlier builds were published from a
          separate binary-only repo that existed only while the source was
          private, and are not carried over.
        -->
        <item>
            <title>0.5.24-beta.9</title>
            <pubDate>Sat, 14 Nov 2026 12:00:48 +0800</pubDate>
            <link>https://github.com/jizhi0v0/duo-updater/releases/tag/v0.5.24-beta.9</link>
            <sparkle:channel>beta</sparkle:channel>
            <sparkle:version>150</sparkle:version>
            <sparkle:shortVersionString>0.5.24-beta.9</sparkle:shortVersionString>
            <sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>15.0</sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>
            <sparkle:hardwareRequirements>arm64</sparkle:hardwareRequirements>
            <description sparkle:format="markdown"><![CDATA[**Supported PKG updates can install directly with the approved helper.** Eligible apps can also update automatically; packages that cannot use the helper still open macOS Installer.

**Temporary download failures recover more reliably.** Automatic updates respect server retry times and retry eligible temporary failures, while failures that need attention pause that version.

**Automatic-update choices are easier to understand.** Per-app explanations distinguish saved choices, defaults and suggestions, including updates only while an app is closed.

**QQ Music update checks and release notes work again.**

**Idle VMPal MCP connections no longer block updates.** Running virtual machines continue to prevent installation.

**More command-line tools show structured release notes.** Support now includes Azure CLI and Codex, more Homebrew packages, Node managed by mise and Ruby managed by rbenv.
]]></description>
